WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:04.100
This kettle costs nine pounds to make.

2
00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:09.700
Sixty-two pence of that could go, and most buyers would never notice.

3
00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:17.610
Across a quarter of a million kettles, that's a hundred and fifty-five thousand pounds. Every year.

4
00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:23.140
It isn't hiding in the price. It's hiding in the design.

5
00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:27.020
Value engineers find it with a method.

6
00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:30.730
See the product as a set of jobs.

7
00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:34.330
Take the competition apart.

8
00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:37.560
Cost every layer honestly.

9
00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:40.640
Then out-think the design.

10
00:00:40.990 --> 00:00:50.680
It's how IBM cut a printer from a hundred and fifty-two parts to thirty-two, and how US highway projects found one point seven billion dollars a year.

11
00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:59.330
Thirteen narrated modules. Labs, not lectures. And you finish with your own value study.

12
00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:04.620
Plus a certificate anyone can check. All free.

13
00:01:04.970 --> 00:01:09.020
Find the cost hiding in every product.
